        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(clawhub): keep request deadline through response body",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes a gap where ClawHub request deadlines were cleared at HTTP headers, leaving stalled or dripping response bodies unbounded. Fixes a compatibility issue where the previous revision applied the same 30s wall-clock deadline to large (up to 256 MiB) archive downloads, which could terminate a healthy progressing transfer.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`clawhubRequest` previously cleared its `AbortController` timer as soon as `fetch` returned headers, so `readResponseWithLimit` per-chunk idle detection was the only body bound — a slow drip could keep resetting chunk-idle and hang forever.\n\nThis change keeps the wall-clock deadline through body consumption for all paths, but archive downloads (`downloadClawHubPackageArchive`, `downloadClawHubSkillArchive`, `downloadClawHubSkillArchiveUrl`, `downloadClawHubGitHubSkillArchive`) release it after headers via a new `releaseAfterHeaders` option. Per-chunk idle detection in `readClawHubResponseBytes` still bounds stalls for all paths.\n\nNon-goals: changing `readClawHubResponseBytes` or `readResponseWithLimit` internals, changing the default 30s budget.\n\nCollision check: no open PR on `src/infra/clawhub.ts` with overlapping deadline semantics.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Stalled or continuously dripping ClawHub metadata/JSON responses fail with the request wall-clock deadline instead of hanging.\n- Archive downloads (skill, package, ClawPack, GitHub source) are not cut off at the 30s metadata budget; a progressing transfer completes while per-chunk idle detection still terminates stalled bodies.\n- Retry, error-body, and JSON paths keep the full-body wall-clock.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `ecb99af3b605822264d8e0c1d8a76db8f8dcd026`\n\n`oxfmt --check src/infra/clawhub.ts src/infra/clawhub.test.ts` — passed.\n`git diff --check` — clean.\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/clawhub.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/clawhub.test.ts > clawhub helpers > keeps the ClawHub request deadline through stalled bodies after headers 53ms\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/clawhub.test.ts > clawhub helpers > aborts ClawHub JSON bodies that drip past the request deadline 52ms\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/clawhub.test.ts > clawhub helpers > times out and cancels stalled skill archive body reads 11ms\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/clawhub.test.ts > clawhub helpers > times out and cancels stalled package archive body reads 8ms\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/clawhub.test.ts > clawhub helpers > times out and cancels stalled ClawPack artifact body reads 8ms\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/clawhub.test.ts > clawhub helpers > lets a progressing archive body survive past the request deadline 6ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  83 passed | 2 skipped (85)\n```\n\n### Contract\n\n| Path | Wall-clock | Chunk-idle | Stall bound |\n|------|-----------|------------|-------------|\n| Metadata/JSON (`fetchJson`, `parseClawHubJsonBody`) | 30s request deadline | 30s | wall-clock |\n| Error bodies (`readErrorBody`) | 30s request deadline | 30s | wall-clock |\n| Skill card (`fetchClawHubSkillCard`) | 30s request deadline | 30s | wall-clock |\n| Promotions feed (`fetchClawHubPromotionsFeed`) | 30s request deadline | 30s | wall-clock |\n| **Archive downloads** | **released at headers** | 30s | **chunk-idle** |\n\n### New test: progressing archive survives past request deadline\n\n- `downloadClawHubSkillArchive` with `timeoutMs: 50`, `releaseAfterHeaders: true`, body drips every 10ms (10 chunks) via fake timers\n- `abortCount: 0` — request deadline was not triggered\n- Transfer completes with valid `sha256Hex` — progressing body not falsely terminated\n\n### Not tested\n\nLive ClawHub CDN against real archive endpoints — requires real ClawHub auth token.",
